# Copy to .env and fill in. The Makefile loads .env, and Conductor copies
# .env* files into new workspaces. `make worktree` copies it into each task
# worktree and adds KNOWSEEK_WORKSPACE, which names that worktree's databases.
# Do not set KNOWSEEK_WORKSPACE by hand in the main checkout.

# Embedding provider: hashing (default, no semantics), ollama (free, local:
# `brew install ollama`, `brew services start ollama`, then `make ollama`),
# or voyage (hosted, needs VOYAGE_API_KEY).
# After a switch, run `make db-reset`. Re-ingesting does not help: ingest skips
# documents whose body is unchanged (see docs/tasks/017-re-embed-job.md).
EMBEDDINGS_ADAPTER=hashing

# Ollama. The model must output 1024 dimensions.
# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=bge-m3
# With `docker compose --profile app up`, localhost is the container itself, so
# the app service reads APP_OLLAMA_URL instead of OLLAMA_URL. The default,
# http://host.docker.internal:11434, reaches Ollama on the host.
# APP_OLLAMA_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# Voyage AI.
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=
# VOYAGE_MODEL=voyage-3.5

# API keys for future providers, for example:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# App container (`docker compose --profile app up --build`). See README.md.
# APP_PORT=4000                    # host port of the API
# APP_DB_NAME=knowseek_prod        # database the container creates and migrates
# SECRET_KEY_BASE=                 # mix phx.gen.secret; compose has an insecure local default
# PHX_HOST=localhost               # public host name, used to build URLs
